{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>When one makes a special vow.</b> One who separates oneself or does an extraordinary thing, for most people follow their desires." "<b>A nazirite vow.</b> Meaning, a vow to be a nazirite, for 'nazirite' is an epithet of the Name." "<b>Nazirite</b> is from the root of וינזרו — that one distances from desires, and does this for the service of HaShem, for wine corrupts the mind and the service of HaShem. And in the section 'When you go out to camp' [Deuteronomy 23:10ff], a hidden meaning is stored away for you."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {2 "The phrase מחנה ארמוז appears to combine 'camp' (מחנה) with an otherwise unknown word ארמוז; rendered hyper-literally as the section heading plus 'a hidden meaning is stored away for you,' reflecting possible corruption or a cryptic allusion Ibn Ezra intentionally leaves obscure."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:16:30.807919026Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}